    "created_at": "2021-10-06T17:52:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-10-06T17:52:16Z",
    "body": "I have never stumbled over this with radio buttons, but I do have a use-case for the `<select>`:\r\nAn option used to be valid, and was selected for this particular form, but has since become invalid for new instances of whatever is being edited.\r\nIt makes sense to communicate this with a `disabled` and `selected` `<option>`, but also allow (or even encourage) the user to switch to one of the still valid options.\r\nI could see this same use-case also applying to radio buttons.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
